   "title": "1066: three kings in one year",
   "text": "Edward the Confessor died childless in January 1066. Harold Godwinson took the crown, beat a Norwegian invasion at Stamford Bridge in September, and was killed at Hastings 19 days later. William of Normandy was crowned on Christmas Day. Norman lords replaced most of the English nobility.",
