   "title": "One king, then one kingdom",
   "text": "In 1603 James VI of Scotland inherited England from his cousin Elizabeth I: one king, two kingdoms. Parliament beheaded his son Charles I in 1649 and ruled without a king until 1660. In 1688 it replaced James II with his daughter Mary and her Dutch husband William. In 1707 England and Scotland became one Kingdom of Great Britain, joined by Ireland in 1801.",
