   "title": "1714: a German king",
   "text": "To keep Catholics off the throne, the Act of Settlement of 1701 passed the crown to Sophia of Hanover and her heirs. Her son George, Elector of Hanover, became king in 1714, and Britain and Hanover shared a ruler for 123 years. The link broke in 1837: Hanover did not accept a queen, so Victoria's uncle became its king.",
