   "title": "1917: the Windsors",
   "text": "Victoria's son Edward VII took his father's house name, Saxe-Coburg and Gotha. In 1917, with Britain at war with Germany, George V renamed the house after Windsor Castle. Edward VIII abdicated in 1936; Elizabeth II reigned for 70 years, longer than any other British monarch. Her son became Charles III in 2022.",
